id: pm-bu8lkr
title: "The eager command barrel in sdk/runtime.ts defeats ADR pm-irp1: 437ms of every invocation is module loading the command cannot use"
description: "src/cli/main.ts has zero dynamic imports and statically imports PmClient from sdk/runtime.ts, a 3,982-LOC barrel with 69 static imports and 0 dynamic imports that costs 437ms of the ~460ms every non---version pm invocation spends before doing any work."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[6]: adr-conformance,agent-ux,"area:cli","area:sdk",performance,startup
created_at: "2026-07-26T18:25:19.540Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T18:31:41.376Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 960
acceptance_criteria: "src/cli/main.ts dispatches every command handler through a dynamic import rather than a static import of a command barrel; Importing the module that constructs PmClient no longer transitively loads runTest, runTestAll, runInit, runTelemetry, or the extension scaffolder; A cold-process measurement of a point read (pm get) on the live workspace shows total wall time reduced by at least the 437ms currently attributable to sdk/runtime.js import; The public SDK export surface and all documented subpath entrypoints are byte-identical before and after the split"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Sub-second becomes sub-300ms for point reads
value: "Restores the cold-start strategy the project already ratified, making every agent command feel instant instead of ~1s."
impact: Every pm command on every host in every session pays this; it is the dominant term in the latency the user experiences as 'not instant'.
outcome: PmClient construction requires no command handler; per-command handlers load through dynamic import in the main.ts dispatch layer; public SDK surface unchanged.
why_now: "Agents invoke pm hundreds of times per session; 437ms x every call is the single largest fixed cost in the tool, and the ADR that was supposed to prevent it is closed and Accepted."
parent: pm-9rxu
risk: medium
confidence: high
dependencies[6]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind}:
  pm-38bskj,related,"2026-07-26T18:29:04.327Z",null,null
  pm-3mal,discovered_from,"2026-07-26T18:29:04.327Z",null,null
  pm-801d,related,"2026-07-26T18:29:04.327Z",null,null
  pm-ag9nka,related,"2026-07-26T18:29:04.327Z",null,null
