  pm-yse5dt,related,"2026-07-26T18:29:04.327Z",null,null
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T18:31:41.375Z","harness:claude-code","A ratified, closed ADR is an audit oracle, not just a record. ADR pm-irp1 decided cold-start would be optimized by lazy per-command imports through a thin dispatch layer in src/cli/main.ts rather than a single large command barrel. Diffing that decision against the current tree found the barrel it forbade (src/sdk/runtime.ts, 3,982 LOC, 69 static imports, 0 dynamic imports) costing 437ms of every invocation, and main.ts containing zero dynamic imports. Neither the closed budget item pm-yse5dt nor the --profile instrument surfaced it: --profile starts inside the handler and reported 235ms for a 939ms pm get, and the budget item measured a floor without owning the module that sets it. The generalizable move is to treat every closed Decision as a conformance test against HEAD, because a decision that was never implemented leaves no failing test and no open item behind it."
body: "## Conformance gap against a ratified ADR\n\nADR pm-irp1 (closed, \"Accepted\") decided cold-start is optimized by\n\"lazy-importing each command's own module through a thin dispatch layer in\nsrc/cli/main.ts **rather than eagerly loading a single large command barrel**\".\n\nThat barrel exists anyway, and it is src/sdk/runtime.ts.\n\n## Measured evidence (2026-07-26, real workspace, 2,101 items)\n\nWall-clock, best of 3, warm:\n\n| invocation | wall |\n|---|---|\n| pm --version (fast path, short-circuits before dispatch) | 73 ms |\n| pm get pm-96h7 | 939 ms |\n| pm list-open --limit 20 | 996 ms |\n| pm search graph --limit 5 | 1156 ms |\n| pm context --limit 5 | 1316 ms |\n| pm next --limit 5 | 1381 ms |\n\nModule-graph cost measured in isolation with a bare node import:\n\n| module | import cost |\n|---|---|\n| node -e \"\" baseline | 44 ms |\n| dist/sdk/runtime.js | **437 ms** |\n| dist/sdk/index.js (barrel) | 462 ms |\n| dist/cli/main.js | 459 ms |\n\nSo ~460 ms of every non-version invocation is module loading, and\n**src/sdk/runtime.ts alone accounts for 437 ms of it**. pm get reports\nprofile:command=get took_ms=235 for the same invocation that costs 939 ms\nwall — the unmeasured remainder is this import (see pm-ag9nka for why the\ninstrument cannot see it).\n\n## Mechanism\n\n- src/sdk/runtime.ts is 3,982 LOC, the largest file in the repository.\n- It has **69 static imports and 0 dynamic imports**.\n- It eagerly pulls every command implementation, including ones the current\n  invocation cannot use: runTest + runTestAll (sdk/test/execution 155 ms,\n  sdk/test/batch 156 ms), runInit (sdk/init 224 ms), runConfig, runTelemetry\n  (72 ms), runDeps, runDocs, runFiles, runList.\n- src/cli/main.ts contains **zero occurrences of \"await import(\"** — the thin\n  lazy dispatch layer the ADR specified was never built (or has regressed) —\n  and it statically imports PmClient from ../sdk/runtime.js at main.ts:82.\n- 15 modules statically import sdk/runtime.js, so no consumer can opt out.\n\nNet effect: `pm get`, a single-item point read, pays for the linked-test\nrunner, the telemetry runtime, the workspace initializer and the extension\nscaffolder before it reads one file.\n\n## Why this is not an existing item\n\n- pm-yse5dt (CLOSED) owned the per-invocation bootstrap *budget and gate*, and\n  the CLI-minus-SDK transport delta. It measured the floor; it did not own the\n  module that sets it.\n- pm-38bskj (CLOSED) owned the *shape of the public SDK export surface*\n  (881 exports, one flat entry). This is the CLI's internal command barrel, a\n  different module and a different axis.\n- pm-3mal (CLOSED) deferred three specific eager startup items (completion\n  flag-strings, MCP tool schema build, telemetry flush spawn) — not the\n  command-handler graph.\n- pm-801d (open) is the data-scaling read index, orthogonal to transport.\n\nThis item owns the single mechanism: the eager command barrel that defeats\nADR pm-irp1, and the lazy dispatch layer that has to replace it.\n\n## Direction (not a mandate for the fix)\n\nSplit runtime.ts so PmClient construction does not transitively require any\ncommand handler; route handlers through per-command dynamic import in the\ndispatch layer main.ts already owns; keep the public SDK surface unchanged so\nthis is a pure internal topology change. The 73 ms `--version` path already\nproves the floor achievable once the barrel is off the critical path."
